  "body": "Firefox doesn't propagate it. Blink does, but I'm removing it since it\ncan be a cross-site leak, and blocks fenced frames since it opens a\ncommunication channel. WebKit only propagates it for `.focus()`, but not\nfor the selection API.\n\nNote that even if the contents in the nested browsing contexts are not\nmarked as inert, if the browsing context container is inert, they won't\nrespond to mouse interactions, and they won't be reached by sequential\nnavigation.\n\nFixes #7605.\n\n<!--\nThank you for contributing to the HTML Standard! Please describe the change you are making and complete the checklist below if your change is not editorial.\n-->\n\n- [x] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * Blink interested in doing the change to stop propagating inertness.\n   * WebKit is already not propagating inertness for selections, only for focusability. And [this comment](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/7605#issuecomment-1036345304) supports the spec change.\n   * Gecko is already not propagating inertness.\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/32817 tests this change.\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/32810 tests that contents of inert iframes are still not reached by sequential navigation and they don't respond to mouse interactions.\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chrome: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=1293191\n   * Firefox: already behaves as proposed.\n   * Safari: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=236512\n\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode: Changes](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/7606/interaction.html\" title=\"Last updated on Feb 11, 2022, 5:24 PM UTC (634c952)\">/interaction.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/7606/f42376d...634c952/interaction.html\" title=\"Last updated on Feb 11, 2022, 5:24 PM UTC (634c952)\">diff</a> )",
